## 5. Backend Architecture

**Entry point:** [server.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/server.js) running on **port 3000**

### Hybrid Data Storage

| Data | Storage | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Students, Departments, Certificates | **Blockchain ledger** (via chaincode) | Immutable, tamper-proof, auditable |
| Marks, Courses, Users, Cert Requests | **JSON files** (`data/` directory) | Fast reads, flexible schema, off-chain workflow |
| Wallet identities | **Filesystem** (`wallet/` directory) | Fabric SDK identity management |

### Backend Data Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [users.json](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/data/users.json) | 12 user accounts across 8 roles (bcrypt hashed passwords) |
| [marks.json](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/data/marks.json) | Student marks with grades, status (pending/verified) |
| [courses.json](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/data/courses.json) | 8 CSE courses with faculty assignments |
| [certificate-requests.json](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/data/certificate-requests.json) | Pending/approved certificate requests |

### Key Backend Modules

| Module | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Fabric Gateway | [fabricGateway.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/fabricGateway.js) | Connects to Fabric network, submits/evaluates transactions |
| Fabric CA Client | [fabricCAClient.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/fabricCAClient.js) | Enrolls admin, registers users with Fabric CA |
| Auth Middleware | [middleware/auth.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/middleware/auth.js) | JWT token verification on all protected routes |
| Wallet Sync | [utils/walletSync.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/utils/walletSync.js) | Syncs wallet identities on startup, purges stale certs |
| Event Listener | [eventListener.js](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/eventListener.js) | Listens for blockchain events (StudentCreated, CertificateIssued, etc.) |

### API Routes

| Route | Controller | Operations |
|---|---|---|
| `/api/auth/*` | Auth | Login, register, token refresh |
| `/api/students/*` | Students | CRUD via blockchain chaincode |
| `/api/marks/*` | Marks | Upload (faculty), verify (exam_section), query |
| `/api/courses/*` | Courses | List, create, assign faculty |
| `/api/certificates/*` | Certificates | Issue (blockchain), request, approve/reject |
| `/api/departments/*` | Departments | CRUD via blockchain chaincode |
| `/api/users/*` | Users | List, manage roles |
| `/api/blockchain/*` | Blockchain | Direct chaincode queries |

### Auto-Seeding on Startup
The server auto-seeds student and department data to the blockchain on startup using [evaluateTransaction](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/fabricGateway.js#120-147) (read) to check existence, then [submitTransaction](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend/src/fabricGateway.js#96-119) (write) if missing.

