## 8. Core Workflows

### Marks Workflow
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant F as Faculty
    participant BE as Backend
    participant ES as Exam Section
    participant S as Student

    F->>BE: Upload marks (POST /api/marks/upload)
    Note over BE: Validates: no duplicates, course exists<br/>Auto-assigns semester from course data<br/>Status = "pending"
    BE-->>F: Marks uploaded ✅

    ES->>BE: View pending marks (GET /api/marks/pending)
    BE-->>ES: All pending marks across all courses

    ES->>BE: Verify marks (PATCH /api/marks/:id/verify)
    Note over BE: Status → "verified"
    BE-->>ES: Verified ✅

    S->>BE: View marks (GET /api/marks/:studentId)
    BE-->>S: All marks (verified ones shown in grade sheet)
```

### Certificate Workflow
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Student
    participant BE as Backend
    participant HOD as HOD/Department
    participant BC as Blockchain

    S->>BE: Request certificate (POST /api/certificates/request)
    Note over BE: Status = "PENDING"<br/>Stored in certificate-requests.json

    HOD->>BE: View pending requests
    HOD->>BE: Approve (PUT /api/certificates/requests/:id)
    Note over BE: Status → "APPROVED"

    BE->>BC: IssueCertificate (submitTransaction)
    Note over BC: Certificate stored on-chain<br/>with PDF hash, IPFS hash

    S->>BE: Download certificate PDF
    Note over S: Generated client-side via jsPDF
```

### Certificate Verification (Public)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant V as Verifier (Employer/University)
    participant BE as Backend
    participant BC as Blockchain

    V->>BE: Verify certificate (GET /api/certificates/verify/:id)
    BE->>BC: VerifyCertificate (evaluateTransaction)
    BC-->>BE: Certificate data + validity
    BE-->>V: ✅ Valid / ❌ Revoked / ❌ Not Found
```

---

## 9. Security

| Feature | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Authentication** | JWT tokens with 24h expiry, bcrypt password hashing |
| **Blockchain RBAC** | MSP-based access control in chaincode (NITWarangalMSP, DepartmentsMSP, VerifiersMSP) |
| **TLS** | All Fabric communication is TLS-encrypted |
| **Private Data** | Student PII (Aadhaar, phone) in private collection, passed via transient map |
| **Immutability** | All student records and certificates on blockchain — cannot be tampered |
| **Audit Trail** | [GetStudentHistory](file:///home/aditi/workspace/Academic_RecordsBlockchain/chaincode-go/chaincode.go#1504-1552) returns full version history from blockchain |
| **Events** | Chaincode emits events (StudentCreated, CertificateIssued, etc.) — backend listens for real-time updates |

---

## 10. How to Run

```bash
# 1. Start the Fabric network (Docker containers)
cd ~/workspace/Academic_RecordsBlockchain
./start_network.sh     # or ./network.sh up

# 2. Start the backend
cd ~/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Backend
npm start              # Runs on port 3000

# 3. Start the frontend
cd ~/workspace/Academic-Records-Blockchain-Frontend
npm run dev            # Runs on port 4200

# Login credentials (all passwords: admin123)
# admin / faculty_demo / exam_section_demo / 25CSM2R26 / CSE
```

